# Go errors: wrap on return

On any **`return ..., err`** from API handlers or internal packages, wrap with `errors.Errorf("<action>: %w", err)` from `github.com/muonsoft/errors`.

**Do not use `fmt.Errorf`** for wrapping.

Example: `return errors.Errorf("publish message: %w", err)` instead of `return err`.

Details: skill `golang-errors` (`.agents/skills/golang-errors/SKILL.md`).
